From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: robgallardof <robgallardof@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:02:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Fix transcribe_timeline: timeline times for every clip; PyAV
 decode; pin mcp<2

transcribe_timeline transcribed only the first clip's whole source file and
returned SOURCE times. On any edited timeline the timestamps pointed to the
wrong place and every other clip's speech was missing.

- CursorBridge: /timeline/clips now includes leftOffset (exact source in-point).
- New src/transcript_mapping.py (pure, unit-tested): clip_window() and
  map_to_timeline() re-time each clip's words to where the clip sits on the
  timeline, clamp words cut by the edit and handle mixed frame rates.
- transcribe_timeline transcribes each source file once and returns segments in
  timeline seconds (time_base: "timeline", sources_transcribed).
- _decode_audio(): decode with PyAV ourselves. faster-whisper's loader passes
  metadata_errors= to av.open(), which recent PyAV removed, so every
  transcription failed. Falls back to the path for unusual containers.
- requirements: mcp<2. mcp 2.x renamed FastMCP and the server no longer starts.
- tests/test_transcript_mapping.py: 4 tests (pytest).
